_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.beta4\n- Reproducible in v4.3.stable.steam (77dcf97d8)\n- Not reproducible (the issue is not present) in v3.6.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8) - Windows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe CanvasItem node's \"item_rect_changed()\" signal is not emitting when rect transform change occurs. Tried restarting the editor, soft reloading the script. Can confirm that this is not caused by anything else, because the \"visibility_changed()\" signal work in the same script, but not \"item_rect_changed()\".\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add 2D Node, and a child Sprite2D node.\n2. Attach a new script to the Sprite2D node.\n3. Add icon.svg to the Sprite2D's texture.\n4. On Node Signals window, connect item_rect_changed() signal to the created script.\n5. Add a basic test print code to the _on_item_rect_changed() function.Example code:\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends Sprite2D\n\nfunc _on_item_rect_changed() -> void:\n\tprint(\"ITEM RECT CHANGED\")\n\n```\n6. Try to change the transform of the Sprite2D\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nProject is using 4.3 stable.\n\n[ItemRectChangedNotEmitting.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18893347/ItemRectChangedNotEmitting.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"gpercem","id":81044486,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQ0NDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81044486?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpercem","html_url":"https://github.com/gpercem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpercem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co